#
# This file is used in constructing the random scenes.
# The descriptions below control what constructs and non-contruct items
# are added to random scenes and with what frequency they are added.
# Each of these collections of items is called a "block".
#
# The syntax is:
#   desc weight needs_road road_offset width
#
# where
#   desc is a string with no blank space, possibly a construct name.
#   weight is an integer, giving the relative frequency it appears.
#   needs_road is 'Y' or 'N' and indicates whether the block must connect.
#   road_offset is a float telling how far back in +Z the block must be
#     moved to connect to a road.  Set to zero when the block is fully
#     resizable.
#   width is the width of the construct or scene.  Set to zero when the
#     block is fully resizable.
#
# Blank lines and lines beginning with '#' are ignored.

